{"timestamp":"2026-07-25T06:04:59.482Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The typed converter still leaves an inversion fact (`stringVals(X) = .ValSeq ⇒ X is empty`) that K does not derive automatically. I’m switching to a raw `ValSeq` predicate that unfolds unconditionally at each constructor and a guarded, semantics-derived length projection. This keeps the domain exact while giving the prover the definedness fact it actually needs; the guard is precisely the reference semantics’ `isStrV`.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-25T06:04:59.482Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_03910549af0707ff016a64520853ec81959748efc750c66a8e","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The typed converter still leaves an inversion fact (`stringVals(X) = .ValSeq ⇒ X is empty`) that K does not derive automatically. I’m switching to a raw `ValSeq` predicate that unfolds unconditionally at each constructor and a guarded, semantics-derived length projection. This keeps the domain exact while giving the prover the definedness fact it actually needs; the guard is precisely the reference semantics’ `isStrV`."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f97d6-4dc8-7d83-aae7-cebf9da1b3c7"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-25T06:05:12.580Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_03910549af0707ff016a64520b7694819588bbe40d7e6e36a7","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ROE8ZJN7cYgBH2hUdz0dkaIk","name":"apply_patch","input":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/verification.k\n@@\n-  // A typed representation of exactly the prompt's list-of-strings domain.\n-  syntax StringItems ::= \".StringItems\"\n-                       | siCons(IntSeq, StringItems)\n-  syntax ValSeq ::= stringVals(StringItems) [function, total]\n-  rule stringVals(.StringItems) => .ValSeq\n-  rule stringVals(siCons(CS:IntSeq, REST:StringItems))\n-    => vCons(str(CS), stringVals(REST))\n+  // The prompt's list-of-strings domain, unfolded one ValSeq constructor at a\n+  // time.  isStrV is supplied by the fixed semantics.\n+  syntax Bool ::= onlyStrings(ValSeq) [function, total]\n+  rule onlyStrings(.ValSeq) => true\n+  rule onlyStrings(vCons(V:Val, REST:ValSeq))\n+    => isStrV(V) andBool onlyStrings(REST)\n+\n+  // A total projection used only under isStrV.  Its non-string case makes the\n+  // definition exhaustive but cannot affect a claim in the formal domain.\n+  syntax IntSeq ::= stringCodes(Val) [function, total]\n+  rule stringCodes(str(CS:IntSeq)) => CS\n+  rule stringCodes(_V:Val) => .IntSeq [owise]\n+\n+  // This is the reference rule seqLen(str(CS)) => isLen(CS), generalized under\n+  // the exact fixed-semantics string recognizer.\n+  rule seqLen(V:Val) => isLen(stringCodes(V))\n+    requires isStrV(V)\n+    [simplification]\n \n   // A left-fold summary that exactly follows the program's accumulator update.\n-  syntax Int ::= totalLen(StringItems) [function, total]\n-               | totalLenFrom(Int, StringItems) [function, total]\n-  rule totalLen(ITEMS:StringItems) => totalLenFrom(0, ITEMS)\n-  rule totalLenFrom(ACC:Int, .StringItems) => ACC\n-  rule totalLenFrom(ACC:Int, siCons(CS:IntSeq, REST:StringItems))\n-    => totalLenFrom(ACC +Int isLen(CS), REST)\n+  syntax Int ::= totalLen(ValSeq) [function, total]\n+               | totalLenFrom(Int, ValSeq) [function, total]\n+  rule totalLen(ITEMS:ValSeq) => totalLenFrom(0, ITEMS)\n+  rule totalLenFrom(ACC:Int, .ValSeq) => ACC\n+  rule totalLenFrom(ACC:Int, vCons(V:Val, REST:ValSeq))\n+    => totalLenFrom(ACC +Int isLen(stringCodes(V)), REST)\n \n   // The exact final value left in a Python for-loop target.\n-  syntax Val ::= lastLoopValue(StringItems, Val) [function, total]\n-  rule lastLoopValue(.StringItems, OLD:Val) => OLD\n-  rule lastLoopValue(siCons(CS:IntSeq, REST:StringItems), _OLD:Val)\n-    => lastLoopValue(REST, str(CS))\n+  syntax Val ::= lastLoopValue(ValSeq, Val) [function, total]\n+  rule lastLoopValue(.ValSeq, OLD:Val) => OLD\n+  rule lastLoopValue(vCons(V:Val, REST:ValSeq), _OLD:Val)\n+    => lastLoopValue(REST, V)\n endmodule\n*** Update File: /workspace/spec.k\n@@\n       #loop(\n-        list(stringVals(ITEMS:StringItems)),\n+        list(ITEMS:ValSeq),\n@@\n       ~> Call(\n         Name(\"total_match\"),\n-        list(stringVals(A:StringItems)),\n-        list(stringVals(B:StringItems))\n+        list(A:ValSeq),\n+        list(B:ValSeq)\n       )\n-      => list(stringVals(A))\n+      => list(A)\n@@\n-    requires totalLen(A) <=Int totalLen(B)\n+    requires onlyStrings(A)\n+     andBool onlyStrings(B)\n+     andBool totalLen(A) <=Int totalLen(B)\n@@\n       ~> Call(\n         Name(\"total_match\"),\n-        list(stringVals(A:StringItems)),\n-        list(stringVals(B:StringItems))\n+        list(A:ValSeq),\n+        list(B:ValSeq)\n       )\n-      => list(stringVals(B))\n+      => list(B)\n@@\n-    requires totalLen(A) >Int totalLen(B)\n+    requires onlyStrings(A)\n+     andBool onlyStrings(B)\n+     andBool totalLen(A) >Int totalLen(B)\n endmodule\n*** End Patch\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f97d6-4dc8-7d83-aae7-cebf9da1b3c7"}}}
