220:{"timestamp":"2026-07-25T06:04:59.482Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The typed converter still leaves an inversion fact (`stringVals(X) = .ValSeq ⇒ X is empty`) that K does not derive automatically. I’m switching to a raw `ValSeq` predicate that unfolds unconditionally at each constructor and a guarded, semantics-derived length projection. This keeps the domain exact while giving the prover the definedness fact it actually needs; the guard is precisely the reference semantics’ `isStrV`.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
