  ✓ Stage 3: rebuild clean K definitions and independently rerun all proof claims
  ✓ Stage 4: audit claim adequacy, satisfiability, and real-program pinning
  ✓ Stage 5: inventory and review every semantic and proof-local rule
  ✓ Stage 6: run a fresh, meaningful non-vacuity mutation
  ✓ Stage 7: account for proven versus assumed facts and write REVIEW.md
